  "lesson": {
    "instructions": "Keep the melody at the same pitch as lesson 7. Play G-sharp on high E fret 4 and F-sharp on high E fret 2. For the melody E, use B-string fret 5 instead of open high E: it is exactly the same pitch. Use a comfortable finger for fret 5 and prepare the next string before plucking.\n\nAfter two count-in bars, bars 3-5 practise the three melody positions without bass. Bars 6-9 repeat the short phrase with rest bars. Bars 10-17 play the whole tune twice, with the familiar alternating E/B bass on the first beat of bars 10, 11, 13, 14, 15 and 17. Bass E is open low E; bass B is A-string fret 2.\n\nVertically aligned notes play together. Begin at 45 BPM; adjust the tempo whenever you need.",
